@*
    An empire's politics: what it believes, how it is run, and what it does with the room that
    leaves. The government's name is not chosen — the game works it out from all three — so it is
    shown in the preview rather than given a panel of its own here.

    All three together, because in the sections they are one decision: picking gestalt greys out most
    authorities and about half the civics, and seeing that happen in the same view is the point. The
    lite card takes them one at a time instead, and shows the consequence on the card behind.
*@

<div class="sem-subsections paired">
    <section>
        <h4>@Session.Localizer.Label("ETHICS", "Ethics")</h4>

        <EthicsSection />
    </section>

    <section>
        <h4>@Session.Localizer.Label("GOVERNMENT_AUTHORITY_AND_TYPE", "Authority and Type")</h4>

        @*
            As short as the ethics above it. There are eight authorities and the nomad toggle, which
            is a row or two of icons — a panel four hundred deep to describe them left most of
            itself empty.
        *@
        <AuthoritySection />
    </section>

    <section>
        <CivicsSection />
    </section>
</div>

@code {
    [CascadingParameter]
    public required DesignSession Session { get; set; }
}
